    {
      "name": "Template Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1056,
        -336
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 900,
        "height": 940,
        "content": "## Answer customer support emails in Gmail with AI and a Google Docs knowledge base\n\nAnswer your customers' emails from a knowledge base you write once in Google Docs. When the answer is not there, it asks you, writes the reply from your answer and tells you what to add to the Doc.\n\n### Who's it for\nSmall businesses, online shops and service providers who answer the same customer questions every day.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every new email in your Gmail inbox is checked. Newsletters, spam and automatic messages are skipped.\n2. The AI answers from your knowledge base only. It never guesses prices, dates or policies.\n3. If it can answer, it saves a draft in the customer's thread, or sends it, depending on your settings.\n4. If it cannot, or the topic is sensitive, it emails you. Click **Respond**, write the facts in your own words, and it writes the reply.\n5. It then sends you a ready-to-paste entry for your knowledge base, so next time it answers on its own.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create your knowledge base in a Google Doc. Use the [interview prompt](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oIcMRiOlRwCpZbbjZJokxYanBw07CxlKTMXvQNhnYgc/edit?usp=sharing) with any AI chat to write it.\n2. Fill in **Support Settings**, the control panel of the workflow. Every option lives there: where questions for you go, draft or send mode, and your knowledge base link.\n3. Connect Gmail, Google Docs and Google Gemini, then activate the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\n- Gmail account\n- Google Docs account\n- Google Gemini API key (the free tier works)\n\n### Customization\nStart with `reply_mode` set to `draft` and switch to `send` once you trust the replies. Use the AI model you prefer: replace the three Gemini model nodes with OpenAI, Anthropic or any other chat model."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Section: 1. Catch new emails",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -80,
        -304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 720,
        "height": 708,
